(4) Where it appears to the Authority that a dominant licensee telecommunications systems provider is taking or intends to take any action which has or is likely to have the effect of giving an undue preference to or causing undue discrimination against any person or category of persons, the Authority may, after giving the dominant licensee concerned an opportunity to be heard, direct the licensee by written notice to cease or refrain from taking such action, as the case may be.

