(b) and is otherwise fit for the grant of such degree, diploma, certificate or other award of the institution;
(e) to consider recommendations made to it by boards of institutes, schools and faculties and take appropriate action;
(f) to make proposals to the institution’s Council or Governing Board on matters relating to the conduct of the institution generally; and
(g) to perform such other functions as are conferred upon the Senate or the Academic Committee by this Act or any other written law, the institution’s enabling instrument or as may be prescribed in regulations made under this Act by the Council or the Governing Board.
