(b) remove a liquidator from office;
(c) call for books, documents and assets of the society;
(d) by order in writing, limit the powers of the liquidator under the provisions of the foregoing section;
(e) require accounts to be rendered to him by the liquidator;
(f) procure the auditing of the liquidator’s accounts and authorise the distribution of the assets of the society;
(g) make or order for the remuneration of the liquidator; and Cap. 33 Power of to control liquidation
(h) refer any subject of dispute between a liquidator and any third party to settlement, where the party have assented in writing to be bound by the decision to be given on the dispute.
(2) Decisions made under this section may be enforced as follows-
(a) when made by a liquidator, by any Court of Resident Magistrate having jurisdiction in the same manner as the decree of the court; and
(b) when made by High Court or a Court of Appeal, in the manner of any appeal as aforesaid as a decree of the Court in any suit pending therein.

