(i) monitoring of safety, through adequate maintenance of operations and inspections;
(ii) choice of adequate route avoiding obstacles, peak hours and densely populated areas and hence have a suitable carriage;
(iii) avoiding over loading of chemicals;
(iv) taking precautions consummerte to properties of the chemical;
(b) prepare contingency plans and procedures for managing accidents which shall be presented to the Board for approval; accidents
