32.–(1) A consignment of plants, plant products or other regulated articles in transit shall be cleared by written notice of the Authority upon receipt of a transit application by the importer and subject to the payment of such fees as may be prescribed.
(2) Phytosanitary import requirements of this Act shall not apply to a consignment in transit where the-
(a) consignment has been packed in such a way that there is no risk of the spread of regulated pests that might be present in the consignment;
(b) consignment as well as the accompanying documents comply with the phytosanitary requirements of the country of destination;
(c) phytosanitary certificate of the country of origin is in conformity with the consignment; and
(d) consignment has not been exposed to pests or become infested with pests.

39.–(1) An inspector may, in the discharge of his duties under this Act-
