47.–(1) The Minister, on recommendation of the National Environmental Advisory Committee may declare any area of land which is ecologically fragile or sensitive to be an Environmental Protected Area.
(2) The powers conferred on the Minister under this section shall not extend to cover areas already declared or which may be declared as protected area under any other written law.
(3) In determining whether or not to declare any area as an Environmental Protected Area, the Minister shall have regard to-
(a) representations made by any person or non-governmental organisations with sufficient public or private interest in the area;
(b) the natural features and beauty of the area;
(c) flora and fauna of the area;
(d) the unique or special geographical, physiographical, ecological or historic and cultural features of the area;
(e) any special scientific feature, cultural feature or biological diversity existing in the area;
(f) the interests of the local communities in or around the area; and
(g) the need for the Government to comply with any international obligation under any agreement to which Tanzania is a member.
(4) The management of the Environmental Protected Area shall be vested to the Council.
