(a) any article commonly used for human consumption shall, if sold or offered, exposed or kept for sale, be presumed until the contrary is proved, to have been sold or, as the case may be, to have been or to be intended for sale for human consumption;
(b) any article commonly used for human consumption, and any article commonly used for the manufacture of products for human consumption which is found in any premises or in any vessel, vehicle or container used for the manufacture, storage, transport or sale of that article or those products, shall be presumed, until the contrary is proved, to be intended for sale, or for manufacturing products for sale for human consumption;
(c) any substance capable of being used in the composition or manufacture of any article commonly used for human consumption, which is found in any premises or vessel where that article is manufactured shall, until the contrary is proved, be presumed to be intended for that use;
